{title: Jeanie with the Light Brown Hair}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}

{c: Verse 1}
I [G]dream of [C]Jeanie with the [G]light brown [D7]hair,
[G]Borne like a [C]vapor on the [D7]summer [G]air.
I [G]see her [C]tripping where the [G]bright streams [D7]play,
[G]Happy as the [C]daisies that [D7]dance on her [G]way.

{c: Verse 2}
[D7]Many were the [G]blithe birds that [C]warbled them [G]o'er,
[A7]Many were the [D7]wild notes her [D7]merry voice would [G]pour.
I [G]dream of [C]Jeanie with the [G]light brown [D7]hair,
[G]Floating like a [C]vapor on the [D7]soft summer [G]air.

{c: Verse 3}
I [G]long for [C]Jeanie with the [G]day dawn [D7]smile,
[G]Radiant in [C]gladness, warm with [D7]winning [G]guile.
I [G]hear her [C]melodies like [G]joys gone [D7]by,
[G]Sighing round my [C]heart o'er the [D7]fond hopes that [G]die.
